# Buffer Response Grounding

## When It Applies

Apply this rule whenever a user request is buffer-related (mentions `buffer`, specific buffer classes, buffering flow, or segment buffering behavior).

## Required Response Standard

- Ground buffer-related proposals in the internal buffer documentation before suggesting code edits.
- Reference at least one relevant internal buffer doc in the explanation when proposing or implementing buffer logic changes.
- If the request spans live and offline flows, reference both relevant categories of docs before finalizing the approach.

## Internal Sources

- `docs/internal/liveaudiobuffer-internal.md`
- `docs/internal/livesegmentbuffer-internal.md`
- `docs/internal/livetextbuffer-internal.md`
- `docs/internal/offlineaudiobuffer-internal.md`
- `docs/internal/offlinesegmentbuffer-internal.md`
- `docs/internal/offlinetextbuffer-internal.md`

## Quality Bar

- Do not rely on assumptions when internal docs define the behavior.
- Call out any uncertainty explicitly if the docs do not specify an edge case.
